--   5. isaiah-58-call-the-sabbath-a-delight-the-sabbath-kept-not-cancelled — NT (Mark 2, Hebrews 4) + Tanakh (Exodus 20, Isaiah 56) [free]
--      (★★★ THE anti-antinomian KEYSTONE: the Sabbath KEPT and called a DELIGHT, made for man, the Son of Adam Lord of it — never abolished)
--   6. isaiah-58-delight-thyself-in-yahuah-the-heritage-of-jacob — NT (1 John 2) [free]
--      (★★★ the blessing on the Sabbath-keeper: delight in Yahuah, the two-house covenant inheritance; the obedience filter)
--   7. isaiah-58-the-fast-that-i-have-chosen-extras-the-vain-fast (Sirach) — Extras (Sirach 34) [extras]
--      (NOTE: Sirach 34 witness is folded into THREAD 1; no separate thread 7 — chapter runs SIX curated threads, slot left unused)
--
-- Framing notes:
--   ★★ THE EMPTY FAST REBUKED (THREAD 1): *Wherefore have we fasted, say they, and thou seest not?
--      wherefore have we afflicted our soul, and thou takest no knowledge? Behold, in the day of your
--      fast ye find pleasure, and exact all your labours. Behold, ye fast for strife and debate, and
--      to smite with the fist of wickedness* (58:3-4). The fast that bows the head as a bulrush
--      (58:5) while oppressing is no fast Yahuah chose. Zechariah carries the same lawsuit: *When ye
--      fasted and mourned... did ye at all fast unto me, even to me?* (Zechariah 7:5); *did not ye
--      eat for yourselves?* (7:6). Yahusha rebukes the show-fast: *when ye fast, be not, as the
--      hypocrites, of a sad countenance: for they disfigure their faces, that they may appear unto
--      men to fast* (Matthew 6:16). And Sirach names the vain repentance: *So is it with a man that
--      fasteth for his sins, and goes again, and doeth the same: who will hear his prayer?* (Sirach
--      34:26). This is exposure of heartless ritual, NOT the abolition of fasting — extras-tier thread.
--   ★★★ THE FAST THAT I HAVE CHOSEN (THREAD 2): *Is not this the fast that I have chosen? to loose
--      the bands of wickedness, to undo the heavy burdens, and to let the oppressed go free, and that
--      ye break every yoke?* (58:6) — covenant-mercy and justice, the Torah-life of Deuteronomy 15:7,
--      the works the King names at the judgment: *I was an hungred, and ye gave me meat... I was a
--      stranger, and ye took me in* (Matthew 25:35); *Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one of the
--      least of these my brethren, ye have done it unto me* (25:40). Torah-as-covenant-life, never curse.
--   ★★★ HIDE NOT FROM THINE OWN FLESH (THREAD 3): *Is it not... that thou bring the poor that are cast
--      out to thy house? when thou seest the naked, that thou cover him; and that thou hide not thyself
--      from thine own flesh?* (58:7) — the doers-of-the-word James presses: *If a brother or sister be
--      naked, and destitute of daily food, And one of you say unto them, Depart in peace... ye give
--      them not those things which are needful to the body; what doth it profit?* (James 2:15-16); *Pure
--      religion... is this, To visit the fatherless and widows in their affliction* (James 1:27).
--   ★★ THE REPAIRER OF THE BREACH (THREAD 4): *Then shall thy light break forth as the morning...
--      thou shalt be called, The repairer of the breach, The restorer of paths to dwell in* (58:8,12).
--      The light that breaks forth is the city on a hill: *Ye are the light of the world... Let your
--      light so shine before men, that they may see your good works* (Matthew 5:14,16). The breach
--      repaired is the fallen booth raised: *In that day will I raise up the tabernacle of David that
--      is fallen, and close up the breaches thereof* (Amos 9:11) — the two-house restoration ministry,
--      the broken wall rebuilt.
--   ★★★ CALL THE SABBATH A DELIGHT (THREADS 5-6 — THE KEYSTONE): *If thou turn away thy foot from the
--      sabbath, from doing thy pleasure on my holy day; and call the sabbath a delight, the holy of
--      Yahuah (LORD), honourable... Then shalt thou delight thyself in Yahuah (LORD)... and feed thee
--      with the heritage of Jacob thy father* (58:13-14). The Sabbath is KEPT and called a DELIGHT —
--      never abolished, never a burden. It is the fourth word: *Remember the sabbath day, to keep it
--      holy* (Exodus 20:8); *Yahuah (LORD) blessed the sabbath day, and hallowed it* (20:11) — creation-
--      rooted. Yahusha confirms it kept, not cancelled: *The sabbath was made for man, and not man for
--      the sabbath: Therefore the Son of Adam is Yahuah (Lord) also of the sabbath* (Mark 2:27-28); and
--      Isaiah 56:2 blesses *the son of Adam... that keepeth the sabbath from polluting it*. Hebrews seals
--      the abiding rest: *There remaineth therefore a rest to the people of Elohim (God)* (Hebrews 4:9).
--      The blessing on the keeper is to *delight thyself in Yahuah* and inherit *the heritage of Jacob*
--      — the two-house covenant inheritance. Kept under the filter: *hereby we do know that we know him,
--      if we keep his commandments* (1 John 2:3); *He that saith, I know him, and keepeth not his
--      commandments, is a liar* (1 John 2:4).
--   VERSES WITH NO SEPARATE ADD: v.2 (yet they seek me daily — the preface to the false-fast lawsuit,
--      woven into THREAD 1), v.9 (then shalt thou call, and Yahuah shall answer — the answered-prayer
--      promise that hinges on putting away the yoke, woven into THREADS 2/4), v.11 (a watered garden,
--      a spring of water — the restoration blessing of THREAD 4, in prose). All recorded, none silently
--      skipped. Extras: Sirach 34:25-26 added on the vain fast (THREAD 1); Sirach 34:21-22 (bread of the
--      needy / defraud the labourer) weighed for the true-fast (v.6-7) but held in prose — the Matthew
--      25 / James witness is the load-bearing NT fill there, no extras double-add forced.

CREATE TEMP VIEW _s303_isa58_lookup AS
SELECT e.slug AS edition_slug, b.slug AS book_slug, c.chapter_number, v.verse_number, v.id AS verse_id
  FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON v.chapter_id=c.id JOIN books b ON c.book_id=b.id
  JOIN editions e ON b.edition_id=e.id
 WHERE e.slug IN ('canon','enoch','jubilees','jasher','apocrypha','apocrypha-charles-vol1','pseudepigrapha','adam-eve-conflict','apocalypse-of-abraham','ascension-isaiah','sonnini-acts-29');

INSERT INTO cross_references (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source, note, tier_required)
SELECT sv.verse_id, tv.verse_id, 'manual', i.note, i.tier::content_tier
  FROM (VALUES
    -- THREAD 1 (★★): The empty ritual fast rebuked (fasting while oppressing is no fast)
    ('canon','isaiah',58,3,'canon','matthew',6,16,'free',
      E'*Moreover when ye fast, be not, as the hypocrites, of a sad countenance: for they disfigure their faces, that they may appear unto men to fast. Verily I say unto you, They have their reward* (Matthew 6:16). *Wherefore have we fasted, say they, and thou seest not?... Behold, in the day of your fast ye find pleasure, and exact all your labours* (Isaiah 58:3) — the same self-serving, show-fast Yahusha rebukes. The hypocrite''s fast for appearance is the very fast Isaiah exposes as empty: a ritual that seeks reward from men, not the mercy Yahuah chose.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',58,5,'canon','matthew',6,17,'free',
      E'*But thou, when thou fastest, anoint thine head, and wash thy face; That thou appear not unto men to fast, but unto thy Father which is in secret* (Matthew 6:17-18). *Is it such a fast that I have chosen?... is it to bow down his head as a bulrush, and to spread sackcloth and ashes under him?* (Isaiah 58:5) — the bowed head and sackcloth, done to be seen, is not the fast Yahuah chose. Yahusha names the true posture: fast unto the Father in secret, not to appear unto men.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',58,3,'canon','zechariah',7,5,'free',
      E'*Speak unto all the people of the land, and to the priests, saying, When ye fasted and mourned in the fifth and seventh month, even those seventy years, did ye at all fast unto me, even to me?* (Zechariah 7:5). *Wherefore have we fasted, say they, and thou seest not?* (Isaiah 58:3) — the same lawsuit. The people fast and mourn, yet Yahuah asks whether they fasted *unto me*; the fast bent to self is no fast unto Yahuah at all.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',58,3,'canon','zechariah',7,6,'free',
      E'*And when ye did eat, and when ye did drink, did not ye eat for yourselves, and drink for yourselves?* (Zechariah 7:6). *In the day of your fast ye find pleasure, and exact all your labours* (Isaiah 58:3) — the fast turned to self-pleasure. As Zechariah exposes the eating-and-drinking done *for yourselves*, so Isaiah exposes the fast done for pleasure: ritual emptied of the justice it was meant to carry.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',58,5,'apocrypha','ecclesiasticus',34,26,'extras',
      E'*So is it with a man that fasteth for his sins, and goes again, and doeth the same: who will hear his prayer? or what does his humbling profit him?* (Sirach 34:26). *Is it such a fast that I have chosen?* (Isaiah 58:5) — Sirach names the same vanity: the fast that humbles the body while the man returns to his sin profits nothing, and his prayer is not heard. The afflicted soul without turned conduct is the empty fast Isaiah rebukes.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',58,4,'apocrypha','ecclesiasticus',34,25,'extras',
      E'*He that washeth himself after the touching of a dead body, if he touch it again, what availeth his washing?* (Sirach 34:25). *Ye fast for strife and debate, and to smite with the fist of wickedness: ye shall not fast as ye do this day, to make your voice to be heard on high* (Isaiah 58:4) — the washing undone by re-touching the corpse is the fast undone by the fist of wickedness. The ritual cleansing that does not change the conduct avails nothing; the voice of such a fast is not heard on high.'),

    -- THREAD 2 (★★★): The fast that I have chosen — loose the bands of wickedness (the true fast = mercy)
    ('canon','isaiah',58,6,'canon','matthew',25,35,'free',
      E'*For I was an hungred, and ye gave me meat: I was thirsty, and ye gave me drink: I was a stranger, and ye took me in* (Matthew 25:35). *Is not this the fast that I have chosen? to loose the bands of wickedness, to undo the heavy burdens, and to let the oppressed go free, and that ye break every yoke?* (Isaiah 58:6) — the fast Yahuah chose IS these works. The mercy that frees the oppressed and breaks the yoke is the very meat-to-the-hungry, welcome-to-the-stranger the King names at the judgment.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',58,6,'canon','matthew',25,36,'free',
      E'*Naked, and ye clothed me: I was sick, and ye visited me: I was in prison, and ye came unto me* (Matthew 25:36). *To loose the bands of wickedness... and to let the oppressed go free, and that ye break every yoke* (Isaiah 58:6) — the chosen fast is covenant-mercy enacted: the naked clothed, the prisoner visited, the oppressed freed. The true fast and the King''s commendation are the same deeds of justice.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',58,6,'canon','matthew',25,40,'free',
      E'*And the King shall answer and say unto them, Verily I say unto you, Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one of the least of these my brethren, ye have done it unto me* (Matthew 25:40). *Is not this the fast that I have chosen?... to let the oppressed go free* (Isaiah 58:6) — the mercy done to the least is done unto the King himself. The chosen fast is not ritual abstinence but covenant-love to the brother; done to the least, it is done to Yahuah.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',58,7,'canon','deuteronomy',15,7,'free',
      E'*If there be among you a poor man of one of thy brethren within any of thy gates... thou shalt not harden thine heart, nor shut thine hand from thy poor brother* (Deuteronomy 15:7). *Is it not to deal thy bread to the hungry, and that thou bring the poor that are cast out to thy house?* (Isaiah 58:7) — the chosen fast is the Torah-mercy of Deuteronomy 15: the open hand to the poor brother. Isaiah does not invent a new ethic; he calls Israel back to the covenant command of the open heart and the open hand.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',58,7,'canon','deuteronomy',15,11,'free',
      E'*For the poor shall never cease out of the land: therefore I command thee, saying, Thou shalt open thine hand wide unto thy brother, to thy poor, and to thy needy, in thy land* (Deuteronomy 15:11). *That thou hide not thyself from thine own flesh* (Isaiah 58:7) — the command to open the hand wide to the brother is the fast Yahuah chose. To hide from thine own flesh is to shut the hand the Torah commands open; the true fast is the covenant generosity of Deuteronomy 15.'),

    -- THREAD 3 (★★★): Hide not from thine own flesh — pure religion, the doers of the word
    ('canon','isaiah',58,7,'canon','james',2,15,'free',
      E'*If a brother or sister be naked, and destitute of daily food* (James 2:15). *When thou seest the naked, that thou cover him; and that thou hide not thyself from thine own flesh* (Isaiah 58:7) — James presses the very case Isaiah names: the brother naked and without daily bread. The chosen fast covers the naked; the dead faith leaves him uncovered.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',58,7,'canon','james',2,16,'free',
      E'*And one of you say unto them, Depart in peace, be ye warmed and filled; notwithstanding ye give them not those things which are needful to the body; what doth it profit?* (James 2:16). *Is it not to deal thy bread to the hungry... when thou seest the naked, that thou cover him?* (Isaiah 58:7) — the word that warms and fills with speech but not bread profits nothing. Isaiah''s true fast and James''s living faith are one: mercy DONE, not merely spoken; the doer, not the hearer only.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',58,7,'canon','james',1,27,'free',
      E'*Pure religion and undefiled before Elohim (God) and the Father is this, To visit the fatherless and widows in their affliction, and to keep himself unspotted from the world* (James 1:27). *To deal thy bread to the hungry, and that thou bring the poor that are cast out to thy house* (Isaiah 58:7) — the fast Yahuah chose IS pure religion: tending the afflicted, the fatherless, the widow. Not ritual, but covenant-mercy to the cast-out — the same worship Isaiah and James both name.'),

    -- THREAD 4 (★★): The repairer of the breach — thy light break forth (restoration of the obedient)
    ('canon','isaiah',58,8,'canon','matthew',5,14,'free',
      E'*Ye are the light of the world. A city that is set on an hill cannot be hid* (Matthew 5:14). *Then shall thy light break forth as the morning, and thine health shall spring forth speedily* (Isaiah 58:8) — the light that breaks forth on the merciful is the light of the city on a hill. The obedient who feed the hungry and free the oppressed become a light that cannot be hid; their righteousness goes before them.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',58,10,'canon','matthew',5,16,'free',
      E'*Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven* (Matthew 5:16). *If thou draw out thy soul to the hungry... then shall thy light rise in obscurity, and thy darkness be as the noonday* (Isaiah 58:10) — the light rising in obscurity is the light shining before men through good works. The mercy done to the hungry is the very good work that makes the light shine and glorifies the Father.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',58,12,'canon','amos',9,11,'free',
      E'*In that day will I raise up the tabernacle of David that is fallen, and close up the breaches thereof; and I will raise up his ruins, and I will build it as in the days of old* (Amos 9:11). *Thou shalt raise up the foundations of many generations; and thou shalt be called, The repairer of the breach, The restorer of paths to dwell in* (Isaiah 58:12) — the repairer of the breach does the work Amos foretells: the fallen booth of David raised, the breaches closed. The restoration ministry rebuilds the broken wall and gathers the scattered house to dwell.'),

    -- THREAD 5 (★★★ KEYSTONE): Call the sabbath a delight — the Sabbath kept, not cancelled
    ('canon','isaiah',58,13,'canon','exodus',20,8,'free',
      E'*Remember the sabbath day, to keep it holy* (Exodus 20:8). *Call the sabbath a delight, the holy of Yahuah (LORD), honourable* (Isaiah 58:13) — Isaiah does not loosen the fourth word; he calls Israel to keep it AS a delight. The Sabbath to be remembered and kept holy is the very *holy of Yahuah* to be called a delight; the command stands, the heart toward it is gladdened.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',58,13,'canon','exodus',20,11,'free',
      E'*For in six days Yahuah (LORD) made heaven and earth, the sea, and all that in them is, and rested the seventh day: wherefore Yahuah (LORD) blessed the sabbath day, and hallowed it* (Exodus 20:11). *Call the sabbath a delight, the holy of Yahuah (LORD)* (Isaiah 58:13) — the Sabbath is creation-rooted, blessed and hallowed by Yahuah himself. What Yahuah blessed and hallowed at creation Isaiah calls Israel to delight in; the holy day is not abolished but honoured.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',58,13,'canon','isaiah',56,2,'free',
      E'*Blessed is the man that doeth this, and the son of Adam that layeth hold on it; that keepeth the sabbath from polluting it, and keepeth his hand from doing any evil* (Isaiah 56:2). *If thou turn away thy foot from the sabbath, from doing thy pleasure on my holy day* (Isaiah 58:13) — Isaiah twice blesses the Sabbath-keeper. The man who keeps the sabbath from polluting it (56:2) is the one who turns his foot from doing his pleasure on the holy day (58:13); the keeping is the blessing, not a burden lifted.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',58,13,'canon','mark',2,27,'free',
      E'*And he said unto them, The sabbath was made for man, and not man for the sabbath* (Mark 2:27). *Call the sabbath a delight, the holy of Yahuah (LORD), honourable* (Isaiah 58:13) — Yahusha affirms the Sabbath KEPT, made for man''s good, not cancelled. The delight Isaiah commands is the gift Yahusha names: the Sabbath made FOR man, a holy day to be honoured, never a yoke to be cast off.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',58,13,'canon','mark',2,28,'free',
      E'*Therefore the Son of Adam is Yahuah (Lord) also of the sabbath* (Mark 2:28). *Doing thy pleasure on my holy day... not doing thine own ways, nor finding thine own pleasure* (Isaiah 58:13) — the holy day is Yahuah''s, and the Son of Adam is Yahuah of it. The Formed Son is Lord OF the Sabbath, not its abolisher; he is its keeper and its Lord, the One whose holy day Isaiah commands be honoured.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',58,13,'canon','hebrews',4,9,'free',
      E'*There remaineth therefore a rest to the people of Elohim (God)* (Hebrews 4:9). *Call the sabbath a delight, the holy of Yahuah (LORD), honourable* (Isaiah 58:13) — the sabbath-rest is not past but REMAINS for the people of Elohim. The delight Isaiah commands is the rest that abides; the keeping of the holy day reaches forward to the rest that remaineth, never cancelled.'),

    -- THREAD 6 (★★★): Delight thyself in Yahuah — the heritage of Jacob (the blessing, the filter)
    ('canon','isaiah',58,14,'canon','1-john',2,3,'free',
      E'*And hereby we do know that we know him, if we keep his commandments* (1 John 2:3). *Then shalt thou delight thyself in Yahuah (LORD)... and feed thee with the heritage of Jacob thy father* (Isaiah 58:14) — the blessing follows the keeping. To delight in Yahuah and inherit the heritage of Jacob is for the one who keeps the holy day; the filter holds: we know him IF we keep his commandments, and the Sabbath-keeper inherits the covenant.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',58,14,'canon','1-john',2,4,'free',
      E'*He that saith, I know him, and keepeth not his commandments, is a liar, and the truth is not in him* (1 John 2:4). *If thou turn away thy foot from the sabbath... then shalt thou delight thyself in Yahuah (LORD)* (Isaiah 58:13-14) — the delight is conditioned on the keeping. He that claims Yahuah but keeps not his commandment is a liar; the heritage of Jacob is fed to the doer, not the one who casts off the holy day while professing to know him.')
  ) AS i(src_edition,src_slug,src_ch,src_v,tgt_edition,tgt_slug,tgt_ch,tgt_v,tier,note)
  JOIN _s303_isa58_lookup sv ON sv.edition_slug=i.src_edition AND sv.book_slug=i.src_slug AND sv.chapter_number=i.src_ch AND sv.verse_number=i.src_v
  JOIN _s303_isa58_lookup tv ON tv.edition_slug=i.tgt_edition AND tv.book_slug=i.tgt_slug AND tv.chapter_number=i.tgt_ch AND tv.verse_number=i.tgt_v
 WHERE sv.verse_id <> tv.verse_id
ON CONFLICT (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 1 (★★) — extras tier (Sirach member)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-58-wherefore-have-we-fasted-the-empty-ritual-fast-rebuked',
       E'Wherefore have we fasted, and thou seest not? — the empty ritual fast rebuked',
       E'The chapter opens with a trumpet-blast against a fast that bows the body while the heart oppresses: *Wherefore have we fasted, say they, and thou seest not? wherefore have we afflicted our soul, and thou takest no knowledge? Behold, in the day of your fast ye find pleasure, and exact all your labours. Behold, ye fast for strife and debate, and to smite with the fist of wickedness... Is it such a fast that I have chosen? a day for a man to afflict his soul? is it to bow down his head as a bulrush, and to spread sackcloth and ashes under him?* (Isaiah 58:3-5). The complaint — *thou seest not* — is answered by exposure: the fast is bent to self-pleasure and to the fist of wickedness, so it is no fast unto Yahuah. Zechariah carries the identical lawsuit: *When ye fasted and mourned... did ye at all fast unto me, even to me?* (Zechariah 7:5); *did not ye eat for yourselves, and drink for yourselves?* (7:6). Yahusha rebukes the show-fast: *when ye fast, be not, as the hypocrites, of a sad countenance: for they disfigure their faces, that they may appear unto men to fast* (Matthew 6:16); fast instead *unto thy Father which is in secret* (6:17-18). And Sirach names the vanity of repentance without changed conduct: *He that washeth himself after the touching of a dead body, if he touch it again, what availeth his washing? So is it with a man that fasteth for his sins, and goes again, and doeth the same: who will hear his prayer? or what does his humbling profit him?* (Sirach 34:25-26). This is the exposure of heartless ritual divorced from justice — NOT the abolition of fasting. The fast itself is good; the fast that smites the brother while it humbles the body is the empty thing Yahuah will not see.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'extras', 27425
  FROM _s303_isa58_lookup sv, _s303_isa58_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=58 AND sv.verse_number=3
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=58 AND ev.verse_number=5
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 2 (★★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-58-the-fast-that-i-have-chosen-loose-the-bands-of-wickedness',
       E'Is not this the fast that I have chosen? — the true fast is covenant-mercy',
       E'Against the empty fast Yahuah sets the fast he DID choose, and it is wholly works of mercy and justice: *Is not this the fast that I have chosen? to loose the bands of wickedness, to undo the heavy burdens, and to let the oppressed go free, and that ye break every yoke? Is it not to deal thy bread to the hungry, and that thou bring the poor that are cast out to thy house? when thou seest the naked, that thou cover him; and that thou hide not thyself from thine own flesh?* (Isaiah 58:6-7). These are exactly the deeds the King names at the judgment: *I was an hungred, and ye gave me meat: I was thirsty, and ye gave me drink: I was a stranger, and ye took me in: Naked, and ye clothed me; I was sick, and ye visited me* (Matthew 25:35-36) — *Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one of the least of these my brethren, ye have done it unto me* (25:40). And Isaiah is calling Israel back to the Torah he already gave: *thou shalt not harden thine heart, nor shut thine hand from thy poor brother* (Deuteronomy 15:7); *Thou shalt open thine hand wide unto thy brother, to thy poor, and to thy needy* (Deuteronomy 15:11). The true fast is not the abolition of Torah but the heart of it — covenant-mercy enacted, the open hand to the brother, the yoke broken off the oppressed. This is Torah-as-covenant-life, never the curse.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27428
  FROM _s303_isa58_lookup sv, _s303_isa58_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=58 AND sv.verse_number=6
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=58 AND ev.verse_number=7
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 3 (★★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-58-hide-not-thyself-from-thine-own-flesh-pure-religion',
       E'Hide not thyself from thine own flesh — pure religion, the doers of the word',
       E'The true fast reaches to the brother in need: *when thou seest the naked, that thou cover him; and that thou hide not thyself from thine own flesh* (Isaiah 58:7). James presses the very same case — and exposes the faith that speaks mercy without doing it: *If a brother or sister be naked, and destitute of daily food, And one of you say unto them, Depart in peace, be ye warmed and filled; notwithstanding ye give them not those things which are needful to the body; what doth it profit?* (James 2:15-16). The word that warms with speech but withholds the bread profits nothing — exactly the empty thing Isaiah''s false fast was. And James names the worship Isaiah commands: *Pure religion and undefiled before Elohim (God) and the Father is this, To visit the fatherless and widows in their affliction, and to keep himself unspotted from the world* (James 1:27). To deal bread to the hungry, to bring the cast-out poor home, to cover the naked, to hide not from one''s own flesh — this is pure religion, the doer of the word and not the hearer only. Isaiah''s true fast and James''s living faith are one and the same covenant-mercy.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27431
  FROM _s303_isa58_lookup sv, _s303_isa58_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=58 AND sv.verse_number=7
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=58 AND ev.verse_number=7
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 4 (★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-58-the-repairer-of-the-breach-thy-light-break-forth',
       E'The repairer of the breach — thy light break forth, the restoration of the obedient',
       E'On those who keep the true fast falls the restoration blessing: *Then shall thy light break forth as the morning, and thine health shall spring forth speedily: and thy righteousness shall go before thee; the glory of Yahuah (LORD) shall be thy rereward* (Isaiah 58:8); *then shall thy light rise in obscurity, and thy darkness be as the noonday... thou shalt be like a watered garden, and like a spring of water, whose waters fail not* (58:10-11). The light that breaks forth is the light of the city on a hill: *Ye are the light of the world. A city that is set on an hill cannot be hid* (Matthew 5:14); *Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven* (Matthew 5:16) — the good works of the chosen fast are the very light that shines. And the obedient earn a name: *thou shalt raise up the foundations of many generations; and thou shalt be called, The repairer of the breach, The restorer of paths to dwell in* (58:12). This is the work Amos foretold: *In that day will I raise up the tabernacle of David that is fallen, and close up the breaches thereof; and I will raise up his ruins, and I will build it as in the days of old* (Amos 9:11) — the fallen booth raised, the breaches closed, the broken wall rebuilt. The repairer of the breach is the restoration ministry that gathers the scattered house and rebuilds the old waste places to dwell in.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27434
  FROM _s303_isa58_lookup sv, _s303_isa58_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=58 AND sv.verse_number=8
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=58 AND ev.verse_number=12
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 5 (★★★ KEYSTONE)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-58-call-the-sabbath-a-delight-the-sabbath-kept-not-cancelled',
       E'Call the sabbath a delight — the Sabbath kept, not cancelled (the keystone)',
       E'The chapter climbs to its climax and the framework''s great Sabbath proof-text: *If thou turn away thy foot from the sabbath, from doing thy pleasure on my holy day; and call the sabbath a delight, the holy of Yahuah (LORD), honourable; and shalt honour him, not doing thine own ways, nor finding thine own pleasure, nor speaking thine own words* (Isaiah 58:13). The Sabbath is to be KEPT and called a DELIGHT — never abolished, never a burden. It is the fourth word, creation-rooted: *Remember the sabbath day, to keep it holy* (Exodus 20:8); *For in six days Yahuah (LORD) made heaven and earth... and rested the seventh day: wherefore Yahuah (LORD) blessed the sabbath day, and hallowed it* (Exodus 20:11). Isaiah twice blesses the keeper: *Blessed is the man that doeth this, and the son of Adam that layeth hold on it; that keepeth the sabbath from polluting it* (Isaiah 56:2). And Yahusha confirms it kept, not cancelled: *The sabbath was made for man, and not man for the sabbath: Therefore the Son of Adam is Yahuah (Lord) also of the sabbath* (Mark 2:27-28) — made FOR man''s good, and the Formed Son is its Lord, not its abolisher. The rest does not pass away: *There remaineth therefore a rest to the people of Elohim (God)* (Hebrews 4:9). The Sabbath blessed and hallowed at creation, commanded at Sinai, delighted in by the prophet, owned by the Son of Adam, and remaining for the people of Elohim — this is the anti-antinomian keystone: the holy day honoured, never thrown away.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27437
  FROM _s303_isa58_lookup sv, _s303_isa58_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=58 AND sv.verse_number=13
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=58 AND ev.verse_number=13
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 6 (★★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-58-delight-thyself-in-yahuah-the-heritage-of-jacob',
       E'Then shalt thou delight thyself in Yahuah — the heritage of Jacob, the blessing on the keeper',
       E'The Sabbath kept opens into the covenant blessing: *Then shalt thou delight thyself in Yahuah (LORD); and I will cause thee to ride upon the high places of the earth, and feed thee with the heritage of Jacob thy father: for the mouth of Yahuah (LORD) hath spoken it* (Isaiah 58:14). The blessing follows the keeping — *if thou turn away thy foot from the sabbath... THEN shalt thou delight thyself in Yahuah* — and the inheritance is *the heritage of Jacob thy father*, the two-house covenant promise to the seed of Jacob. This is the framework''s filter made plain: obedience and blessing are joined, never severed. John seals it: *hereby we do know that we know him, if we keep his commandments* (1 John 2:3); *He that saith, I know him, and keepeth not his commandments, is a liar, and the truth is not in him* (1 John 2:4). The one who delights in the holy day delights in Yahuah and is fed the heritage of Jacob; the one who casts off the commandment while professing to know him is a liar, and the truth is not in him. The heritage of Jacob is for the doer — the Sabbath-keeper, the merciful, the repairer of the breach — never for the lawless professor.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27440
  FROM _s303_isa58_lookup sv, _s303_isa58_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=58 AND sv.verse_number=14
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=58 AND ev.verse_number=14
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

